[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800]   As a reminder, the Rule of 40 is an industry rule of thumb that says a high-growth SaaS
[00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.920]   company can burn as much cash as it likes in order to drive growth, as long as its growth
[00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:13.400]   rate is 40 percentage points higher than its free cash flow margin. It's an attempt at
[00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.480]   devising a simple rule to help software companies with the complex question of how to balance
[00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:19.560]   growth and profitability.
[00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.320]   One past study showed that while Rule of 40 compliance software companies made up a little
[00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:27.260]   more than half of all public software companies that they captured more than half of all public
[00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.860]   software companies that they captured more than 80% of all public market cap.
