[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720]   Less than half of all companies in this set are Rule of 40 compliant. The median Rule of 40 score
[00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:11.920]   was 31.7%. The median multiple for companies in the set was 6.6 times. The slope of the line is 12,
[00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.320]   meaning that for each 10 percentage points of Rule of 40 score improvement, a company's revenue
[00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:22.960]   multiple increases by 1.2 times. R to the 2 is 0.42, which, if I recall correctly, means that the
[00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:28.480]   Rule of 40 score explains 42% of the variability of the data. So, while there's lots it doesn't
[00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:32.640]   explain, it's still a useful indicator. A few nerdier things of note.
