[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.440]   Remember that the line is only valid in the data range presented, since no companies had
[00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:09.220]   a negative rule of 40 score, it would be invalid extrapolation to simply continue the line down
[00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:11.000]   and to the left.
[00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.780]   Early-stage startup executives often misapply these charts for getting the selection bias
[00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.280]   within them.
[00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:19.800]   Every company on the chart did well enough at some point in terms of size and growth
[00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.140]   to become a public SaaS company.
[00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:27.820]   Just because LivePerson LPSN has a 4x multiple within rule of 40 score of 10% doesn't mean
[00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:31.340]   your $20 million start-up with the same score is also worth $4.10.
