[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.280]   As? LPSN is a much bigger company, roughly $250 million, and already cleared many hurdles
[00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:07.280]   to get there.
[00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:11.280]   The big question around the Rule of 40 is, when should companies start to target it?
[00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:17.360]   A superstar like Elastic had 76% growth and 8% FCF margin, so a Rule of 40 score of 84%
[00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:23.680]   at its spectacular IPO. However, Avalara had 26% growth and 28% FCF margin for an Rule
[00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:28.320]   of 40 score of 2% and its IPO went fine, Ditto and Applin.
