[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.240]   I'll be doing some work in the next few months to try and get better data on Rule of 40 trajectory
[00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:05.960]   into an IPO.
[00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:10.720]   My instinct at this point is that many companies target Rule of 40 compliance too early, sacrifice
[00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:14.720]   growth in a process, and hurt their valuations because they fail to deliver high growth and
[00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.920]   don't get the assumed customer acquisition cost efficiencies built in the financial models,
[00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.280]   which end up, as one friend called them, spreadsheet-induced hallucinations.
