[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.600]   I quibble with some of the Bessemerisms in the definition. For example, (1) most enterprise
[00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.760]   SaaS companies should use annual recurring revenue (ARR) not monthly recurring revenue (MRR)
[00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:16.800]   because most enterprise companies are doing annual, not monthly, contracts (2) the committed
[00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:22.000]   MRR concept is an overreach because it includes anticipated churn which is basically impossible
[00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.280]   to measure and often unknown, and (3) I don't know why they use the prior period for both
[00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:33.680]   S&M costs and new ARR. Almost everybody else uses prior period S&M, divided by current period.
[00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.080]   ARR in customer A.
