[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.960]   Project A has a net present value, NPV, of 500 units. Project B has an NPV of 110 units.
[00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:11.600]   Well, don't you feel silly for picking Project B? Payback is all about how long your money is
[00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.600]   committed so it can't be used for other projects, and at risk meaning you might not get it back.
[00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:21.520]   Payback doesn't tell you anything about return. In capital budgeting, NPV tells you about return.
[00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:25.760]   In a SaaS business, customer lifetime value, LTV, tells you about return.
