[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.480]   There are situations where it makes a lot of sense to look at CPP. For example, if you're running a
[00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:08.080]   monthly SaaS service with a high churn rate then you need to look closely how long you're putting
[00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.400]   your money at risk because there is a very real chance you won't recoup your CAC investment,
[00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:17.120]   let alone get any return on it. Consider a monthly SaaS company with a $3,500
[00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:23.360]   customer acquisition cost, subscription gross margin of 70%, a monthly fee of $100, and 3%
[00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:28.720]   monthly churn. I'll calculate the ratios and examine the churn. I'll calculate the ratios
[00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.840]   and examine the CAC recovery of 100 customer cohort.
