[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.960]   Soapbox, this is another case where using a model is infinitely preferable to back-of-the-envelope
[00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.820]   BOTT analysis using SAS metrics.
[00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.520]   If you want to understand the financials of a SAS company, then build a driver-based model
[00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:13.200]   and vary the drivers.
[00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:18.120]   In this case and many others, BOTT analysis fails due to subtle complexity, whereas a
[00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:22.160]   well-built model will always produce correct answers, even if they are counterintuitive.
