[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720]   The CPP formula outputs a payback period in months, but most enterprise SaaS businesses
[00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:09.920]   today run on an annual rhythm. Despite pricing that is sometimes still stated per user per month,
[00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:14.160]   SaaS companies realized years ago that enterprise customers preferred annual contracts and actually
[00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.800]   disliked monthly invoicing. Just as MRR is a bit of a relic from the old SaaS days,
[00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.600]   so is the CAC payback period stated in months.
