[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.640]   In a 100 percent annual prepaid contract world, the CPP formula should output in multiples
[00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:09.440]   of 12, rounding up for all values greater than 12.
[00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:14.440]   For example, if a company's CAC payback period is notionally 13 months, in reality
[00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:19.280]   it is 24 months because the leftover January 13 of the cost isn't collected until the
