[00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:09.680]   then it should be rounded down to one day because you are invoicing the entire year up front and at
[00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:16.400]   once. Even if the formula says the CPP is notionally 12.0 months, in an annual prepaid world your CAC
[00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:22.160]   investment money is at risk for just one day. So, wait a minute, what is the actual CAC payback
[00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.560]   period in this case. 12.0 months or one day. It's one day.
