[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.340]   Anyone who argues 12-to-no months is forgetting the point of the metric.
[00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:07.720]   Payback periods are risk metrics and measured by the amount of time it takes to get your
[00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.200]   investment back.
[00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.040]   If you want to look at S&M efficiency, look at the CAC ratio.
[00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.420]   If you want to know about the efficiency of running the SAAS service, look at subscription
[00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:17.940]   gross margins.
[00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:23.060]   If you want to talk about lifetime value, then look at LTV/CAC.
[00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:28.040]   CAC payback period is a risk metric that measures how long your CAC investment is on the table
[00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.880]   before getting paid back.
[00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.440]   In this instance, the 12 months generated by the S.
