[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.120]   A lot of very smart people get stuck here. They say, "Yes, sure, it's one day, but really it's not. It's 12 months."
[00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:09.280]   No, it's one day. If you want to look at something other than payback, then pick another metric.
[00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:13.120]   But the CPP is one day. You asked how long it takes for the company to recoup the money it
[00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:18.320]   spends to acquire a customer. For CPPs less than or equal to 12 in a 100% annual prepaid world,
[00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:19.520]   the answer is one day.
