[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.280]   it gets harder. Imagine a company that sells in a sticky category, for example, where typical
[00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.600]   lifetimes may be 10 years and thus is a high-consideration purchase where prospective
[00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:15.200]   customers do deep evaluations before making a decision, for example, ERP. As a result of all
[00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.840]   that homework, customers are happy to sign long contracts and thus the company does only 3-year
[00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:26.080]   prepaid contracts. Now let's look at CA/C payback period. Adapting our rules above, any output from
[00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:32.800]   the formula greater than 36 months should be rounded up in multiples of 36 months.
