[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.440]   While I have not yet devised general rounding rules for this situation,
[00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:07.520]   the model again demonstrates the key point. That the mix of one-year and three-year payment
[00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:13.440]   structure confounds the CPP formula resulting in a notional CPP of 24 months, when in reality it
[00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.080]   is again one day. If you want to make rounding rules beware the temptation to treat the average
[00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:23.280]   contract duration (ACD) as a rounding multiple because it's incorrect. While the ACD is two
[00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:27.600]   years in the above example, not a single customer is paying you at two-year intervals, half are
[00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.320]   paying you every year while half are paying you every TD.
