[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.560]   If I wanted to be even more rigorous, I would argue that you should not include subscription
[00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:11.520]   gross margin in the calculation of CAC payback period. If your CAC ratio is 1.0 and you do
[00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:17.520]   annual prepaid contracts, then you immediately recoup 100% of your CAC investment on day one.
[00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:22.240]   Yes, a new customer comes with a future liability attached, you need to bear the
[00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:26.400]   costs of running the service for them for one year, but if you're looking at a payback metric
[00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.520]   that shouldn't matter. You got your money back? Yes, going forward you need to spend about 30%,
[00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.840]   a typical subscription COGS.
