[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.040]   3. The startup ecosystem purge continues. Hit. I got lucky here because I meant to say
[00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.200]   "accelerates," but wrote continues, which is more indicative of what happened.
[00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:15.920]   In 2023, 769 startup shut down. In 2024, that figure rose to 966, and Carda's commentary
[00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:22.320]   suggests the 2025 total will fall between 1,000 and 1,100. Interestingly, per simple closure,
[00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.440]   startups shut down later in their life cycle compared to 2024.
