[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.320]   But an ecosystem purge is also about M&A, not just shutdowns. Per Burberry Noise, 2025,
[00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:12.880]   M&A volume was up 66% from 2025, so 43 billion dollars to 420 billion dollars,
[00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:19.760]   with deal count up 8% from 1922 to 2022. The point was that many startups were going to
[00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:24.640]   hunger down in 2025, extending cash runways to buy time until the return of a healthier exit
[00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:29.680]   environment. That return did not happen in 2025, so many of them will need to keep hungering.
[00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:35.200]   Exit multiples were flat to down in 2025, though I am hopeful they will bounce up in 2026.
