[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.960]   5. The World Wide Web, as we knew it, is dead. Hit.
[00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:07.680]   The Economist called this one for me. Here's what they had to say, artificial intelligence
[00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.920]   is transforming the way that people navigate the web. As users pose their queries to chatbots
[00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.180]   rather than conventional search engines, they are given answers rather than links to follow.
[00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:20.140]   The result is that content publishers from news providers and online forums to reference
[00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:23.180]   sites such as Wikipedia are seeing alarming drops in their traffic.
