[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.880]   9. PR is the new SEO miss
[00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:06.680]   While I think people would acknowledge the underlying point, that great PR hits can have
[00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:10.960]   a strong positive effect on answer engine inclusion. I don't think this realization
[00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:15.940]   sparked the PR renaissance that I was hoping for in 2025. First, because few companies
[00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:20.380]   can generate such a hit regardless of their PR investment, that is, even a great PR flack
[00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:24.740]   needs an articulate and charismatic founder, a product with demonstrable customer impact
[00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:28.800]   and momentum, and a story that maps pretty directly to mainstream business.
[00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.800]   growth and an enormous fundraising round D.
