[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.880]   More importantly, it's because PR has changed.
[00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:07.400]   It's a lot more trench warfare across dozens of bloggers, podcasters, and influencers than
[00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.640]   it is swinging for home run stories.
[00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:14.480]   If any spending shot up in 2025, it was on lobbying, not public relations, though the
[00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.440]   two fields are less far apart than one may think.
[00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:21.520]   But no sane marketer is going to propose a big PR budget in order to boost their AEO
[00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:22.520]   program.
[00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.000]   There are so many other things they can do first.
[00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.720]   So hopefully that was thought-provoking.
[00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:28.320]   But amiss.
