[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.680]   10. LinkedIn enters the social media death cycle.
[00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:04.680]   Partial.
[00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.560]   Followers will know I've been trying to manifest LinkedIn improvement because I've
[00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:12.860]   had troubles remaining on X, and this prediction was kind of a caution, an anti-manifestation,
[00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:17.120]   as if anyone was listening to say if LinkedIn doesn't get better, it might get a lot worse.
[00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.120]   But neither happened.
[00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.200]   It didn't get better, but it didn't really get worse.
[00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.380]   It's still the same vanilla, namby-pamby, excessively self-promoting content as it was
[00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:29.640]   in 2024, but I do see an increasing number of posts from second-hand recyclers of ideas.
[00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:30.760]   Think Steve Jay.
