[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.320]   For example, consider a native. AI company growing 200% that recently raised money at 50 times $20
[00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:13.120]   million in ARR, so a $1 billion valuation. Now, let's say growth slows well below 100%,
[00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:17.680]   but they grind it for 2 to 3 years to double revenues. For a flat round, they'd need a 25
[00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:21.120]   times valuation, but with things deteriorating that's not going to happen.
[00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.160]   So, how can you obscure a down round if you want to?
[00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.360]   Structure. You can put a 2 times liquidation
[00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.840]   preference on the new money to preserve the headline $1 billion valuation, but ceteris
[00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.440]   aren't parabas. This is...
