[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.600]   I think 2026 will see a big uptick relative to 2025, both in the number of transactions
[00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.360]   and the deal sizes. Why? First, because there is a backlog of amazing companies waiting in line.
[00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:15.600]   Second, because while companies can stay private longer, sometimes indefinitely,
[00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.240]   that's becoming the luxury of the ultra-elite firms, so all the merely elite ones will still
[00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:25.440]   need to go public at some point to get proper liquidity. Third, because a better exit environment
[00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:30.240]   is one of the top priorities Trump supporting VCs wanted, and I believe both Sandhill Road
[00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.320]   and Wall Street will apply significant pressure.
