[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000]   And sometimes, when we think a job is going to be automated away, we get it wrong.
[00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:10.000]   In 2016, the godfather of AI, Jeffrey Hinton, said that we should stop training new radiologists
[00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.280]   because AI could read images better than people. And he was right. AI has outperformed people for
[00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:19.760]   nearly a decade at image reading. But today we have more radiologists than ever, with an average
[00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:24.880]   salary of $520,000. It turns out that reading images isn't all that radiologists do.
