[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.880]   People can't trust the algorithms to show them content they want to read.
[00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:07.800]   Slide into the wrong thread and X instantly turns into a bot-driven cesspool of ad hominem
[00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:08.800]   attacks.
[00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.200]   LinkedIn has become a tedious sea of corporate news, thinly veiled pitches, humblebrags,
[00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.040]   and ghost-written content.
[00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:18.080]   Review sites, despite consumer protection rules, are often gamed.
[00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:22.920]   Soon, if not already, we'll be using AI both to generate and summarize our communications.
[00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:28.400]   And, as Scott Brinker says in his predictions, AI inbox gatekeepers will turn email marketing
[00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.040]   into earned media. Ponder that for a second.
