[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160]   I've always felt that branding was simply about trust. Trust that you'll be you. Trust that you'll
[00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:08.400]   look like you visual. Trust that you'll sound like you voice. Trust that you'll act like you values.
[00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.680]   Operating principles. Trust in your mission vision. It's funny.
[00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.360]   The further we got into the internet era, the more we heard that people didn't have time anymore.
[00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.440]   And that long-form content was dead. So, everything needed to be bite-sized morsels.
[00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:23.760]   There's no time. Make it shorter. Make it a short video. Make it a short video. Make it a short
[00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:28.400]   video. Make it a short video. Make it a short video. Make it an infographic. I always believe
[00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.080]   David Augie, Alain, then you got into the internet era. The more we heard that more we heard that more
[00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.760]   we heard that people didn't have time anymore.
