[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.480]   Back in the day, using several assumptions, a successful VC running four funds in parallel
[00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:09.120]   could make around $3 million/year-in-fee income. With that, they could live a very
[00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.920]   comfortable Silicon Valley life—a house in Atherton, a place in Tahoe, tuition at
[00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:18.400]   the Menlo School, and all the rest. But to get really rich, fly your PJ to your
[00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.640]   Montana Ranch Ridge, then you need to carry.
