[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.360]   The second half of the 2 in 20 fee structure common in VC. The 2% is the annual fee on
[00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:11.860]   committed capital. The 20% is the carry, or cut, that VCs take after the fund returns
[00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:17.340]   its initial capital to investors. For example, if a $250 million fund returns three times
[00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:24.000]   to investors, the VCs would make $100 million in carry, 20% of $500 million over the fund's
[00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.240]   roughly 10-year life cycle. Split that $100 million across five general
[00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:32.880]   partners, and after one fund you've got the Montana Ranch and, after another, the PJ to
[00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:33.560]   fly to it.
