[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.680]   But 2% of a huge number is a huge number. So today, with a $5 billion fund, a VC can
[00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.440]   make more money off fees alone than they previously made off fees in Cary.
[00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:15.520]   By my rough math more than double. On top of this, the Cary split across 15 GPs would be $133
[00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:21.280]   million each. While I've spent my career in and around VC-backed startups, I don't consider myself
[00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:26.400]   an expert on VC per se. But I think this new megafund reality changes things. Remember the
[00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.640]   For the Charlie Munger quote, "Show me the incentive and I'll show you the outcome."
