[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.560]   People managing large amounts of money need to deploy it.
[00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:08.560]   You can't raise $5 billion, collect $100 million/year-in fees, and then not invest the money.
[00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:11.240]   They will generally prefer to deploy it in bigger chunks.
[00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:19.000]   It's easier to deploy $5 billion with $250 million to $500 million checks than $25 million to $50 million.
[00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.120]   It's the difference between 20 investments and 200 investments.
[00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:26.920]   There's a fixed cost and a relatively high one in preinvestment diligence and investment diligence.
[00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:28.880]   In investment commitment presentations,
[00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.240]   kingmaking should increase.
[00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:34.560]   If I fovety $1 million to $500 million checks, then $25 million checks,
[00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.760]   then $25 million checks, then $25 million.
[00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.920]   Checks, then 20 investments, and 200 million.
