[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.640]   Whatever reason, that Founder X will be the winner, I can load them up with money to help ensure that
[00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:09.440]   outcome happens. While more VC gets deployed, it ends up being a have and have and have not
[00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:14.480]   financing environment. There will be a temptation to foie gras startups. Unlike the geese, this
[00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:19.200]   requires founders as willing accomplices. But if you follow the simple rule of "raise money when
[00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.520]   you can on good terms," most will say yes. Hopefully, they then won't piss it away,
[00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.440]   which is how you get in real trouble. This should create a "damn the torpedoes" attitude,
[00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.940]   if you need to deploy $5 billion in ORD.
