[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.360]   or to make $20 million/year in fee income, then I'm pretty sure you're going to find a way to do so.
[00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:08.400]   Moreover, if the game becomes "Tales I win big,
[00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.960]   Heads I win five times bigger," then who doesn't want to play?
[00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:15.440]   Put differently, it's not hard to be a techno-optimist when your firm is collecting $300
[00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:21.760]   million/year in fee income off your last $15 billion round of funds. Heck, I'd be one too.
[00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:25.280]   Mega VCs will become more investors and less business partners.
[00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:29.200]   I remember when Sequoia's tagline was "The Entrepreneurs Behind the Entrepreneurs."
