[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720]   As the Tom Lehrer lyric goes, "Once the rockets are up, who cares where they come down?
[00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:07.120]   That's not my department," says Warren Hervon Braun.
[00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:12.000]   But data warehouses taught me to care about technical and operational metadata.
[00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.240]   Data catalogs taught me to care about governance, collaboration, and quality metadata.
[00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.000]   Over time, I became a true believer in context around data.
[00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000]   Thirty years in business taught me to care about business metadata.
[00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.080]   Stuff that, until recently, most of us only dreamed of keeping in systems.
