[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.640]   And their multiples change. Consider this tweet. Looks like we're paying five times sales for
[00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:10.400]   software. Mr. Ballantine has set the price. Let's observe that five times sales with 33%
[00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:17.520]   EBITDA margins means 15 times EBITDA, which by PE standards is a healthy multiple for a
[00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:22.640]   software company. Also remember that five times is about twice the average price/sales ratio
[00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:28.400]   of the S&P 500. So, software companies are still well-valued as they were before. Just not as well
[00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.400]   valued as they were before.
