[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.560]   The Rule of 40 is a SAS metric that was created to be a better predictor of a company's enterprise
[00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:11.840]   value to revenue, EV/R multiple, than growth or EBITDA alone. The intent coming off a growth-crazed
[00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:16.640]   period was that the best company should balance growth and profit. Hence the Rule of 40 was
[00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:21.600]   generally calculated as "Rule of 40 score we revenue growth rate plus FCF margin."
