[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160]   Year later, Bessemer came along and correctly argued that a point of growth should be worth
[00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:09.040]   more than a point of profit, and created the, unfortunately named, Rule of X, which put a slow
[00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:14.880]   varying multiple on growth relative to profit, typically around 2.3 times. Years before, and less
[00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:19.120]   visibly, the Software Equity Group had created a two-times growth-weighted Rule of 40 which did
[00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.880]   roughly the same thing.
