[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.840]   Over the four years, the first company ends up valued at $5.0T million on a 15x FCF basis
[00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:11.360]   and $8.64 million on a 5x sales basis. Since there's a question whether either of those
[00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:16.720]   companies would get valued on a revenue, multiple, which is usually associated with higher growth,
[00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:22.400]   let's look primarily at the FCF multiples. The second company ends up worth $1.03 billion
[00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:28.000]   based on 15x FCF, whereas the first one ends up worth only about half that at $5.0T million.
[00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:34.480]   Since PE investors usually see profit as more of sure thing, that is, more within management.
