[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.960]   In my view, the most consistently monetizable activity in the crypto ecosystem has been
[00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.920]   the promotion and issuance of new tokens.
[00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:12.280]   Given that such tokens usually lack intrinsic value, these dynamics can, in practice, start
[00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.320]   to resemble Ponzi structures.
[00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:19.060]   Moreover, crypto assets have also been associated with a range of questionable and/or illegal
[00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:25.160]   use cases, including money laundering, ransomware, online fraud, and investment scams, political
[00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.680]   influence, tax evasion, and payments for illegal goods.
[00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.440]   Remember how Tim Draper came across his considerable Bitcoin position?
[00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:33.800]   The most legitimate use cases?
