[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.560]   The naming here gets tricky due to existing conventions. If I were to call it net expansion
[00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:10.160]   rate, it would be too easily confused with net revenue retention. NRR, they sound too similar.
[00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:15.440]   What I'm trying to get at is the mechanism through which you hit your NRR. You can hit any given
[00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:22.080]   NRR, for example, 100% in several ways. For example, expansion of 50 against shrinkage of 50,
[00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:27.680]   or expansion of 0 against shrinkage of 0. The first example has a retention shrinkage of 0.
[00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.320]   The first example has a retention spread of 50 points, 100 minus 100s.
