[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520]   Kyle Poyar wrote a nice report, the AI churn wave, on this topic. While he doesn't explicitly look
[00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.000]   at retention spreads, and while his data doesn't show what I'd expect—that is, higher retention
[00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.040]   spreads in AI than B to be SAS—we do both arrive at the same conclusion. There is a wave of churn
[00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:20.480]   in AI startups coming. But launching something on December 22? Was this the ultimate contrarian
[00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.880]   timing? Or a launch that slipped a few weeks and they thought, "Oh, just do it anyway. I no longer
[00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.120]   tell my erstwhile favorite joke, the only thing you can make with metadata is metamagineime.
