[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.600]   Much like how AI was a thing, decades ago, but only became real and widespread recently,
[00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.580]   so had knowledge management been a thing for decades.
[00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.160]   But it's also never been real and mainstream.
[00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:12.800]   Maybe now it finally will.
[00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:17.060]   Similarly, I know that process mining has been around for a while, and Solonus has created
[00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:20.400]   a $113 billion valuation business doing it.
[00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:25.360]   I view this as validation for lighter, more automated, more robust process graphs.
[00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:30.160]   As the William Gibson quote goes, "The future is already here, it's just unevenly distributed."
