[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.540]   Mix of one, two, and three year deals, then your renewal rate isn't a single rate at
[00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.340]   all, but a matrix.
[00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.460]   Do you want to explain that to investors?
[00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:10.980]   T you up for price knockoff at sales time?
[00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:15.580]   Some buyers, particularly those in private equity PE, PE, will look at the relatively
[00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:19.940]   large long-term deferred revenue balance as cashless revenue and try to deduct the cost
[00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:21.780]   of it from an acquisition price.
[00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:25.740]   Moreover, if not discussed upfront, someone might try to knock it off what you thought
[00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.340]   was a final number.
[00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:31.780]   And reduce value for strategic acquirers, under today's rules, for reasons that I don't
[00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:32.800]   on on burses.
