[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400]   Tirely understand, deferred revenue seems to get written off and thus never recognized in
[00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:10.240]   a SaaS acquisition. So, ceteris paribus, an acquirer would greatly prefer non-prepaid TCV,
[00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:14.160]   which it will get to recognize over time to deferred revenues, which it won't,
[00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.720]   can give pause to strategic acquirers. Anything that might cause the acquirer to need to start
[00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:23.280]   release pro forma financials has the potential to scare them off, particularly one with otherwise
[00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:27.840]   pristine financial statements. For example, having to explain why revenue from a recently
[00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:33.600]   acquired startup is shrinking year-over-year might.
