[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.840]   Do precisely that. Can inflate revenues. Under ASC 606, multi-year prepaid deals are
[00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:10.560]   seen as significant financing events, so, if I have this correct, revenue will exceed the
[00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:14.080]   cash received from the customer as interest expense will be recorded and increase the
[00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:18.880]   amount of revenue. Some buyers, particularly PE ones, will see this as another form of
[00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:22.480]   cashless revenue and want to deflate your financials to account for it since they are
[00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:28.000]   not primarily concerned with GAAP financials but are more cash focused. We'll similarly inflate
[00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.200]   remaining Performance Obligation (ERPO)
[00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.320]   SaaS companies!
