[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.200]   are increasingly releasing a metric called RPO which I believe is supposed to be a more rigorous
[00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:11.520]   form of what one might call Remaining TCV Total Contract Value. That is, whether prepaid or not,
[00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:15.920]   the value of remaining obligations undertaken in the company's current set of contracts.
[00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:21.520]   If this is calculated on a GAAP basis, you're going to have the same inflation issue as with
[00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:27.520]   revenues when multi-year prepaid deals are involved. For example, I think a 3-year 100-unit
[00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:32.640]   deal done with annual payments will show up as 200 units of RPO, but the same deal done
[00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.240]   on a prepaid basis will show.
