[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.360]   up is 200-something, for example 210, 220, due to imputed interest.
[00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.000]   Impede analysis of billings. If you want to go public or get acquired by a public company,
[00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.600]   financial analysts are going to focus on a metric called calculated billings,
[00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:18.000]   which is equal to revenue plus the change in deferred revenue for a given time period.
[00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.120]   For SaaS purest companies, that is, those that do only annual contracts with one-year prepays,
[00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:26.560]   calculated billings is actually a pretty good measure of new sales.
[00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:31.120]   Multiyear prepays impede analysis of billings because deferred revenue ends up a mishmash
[00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:32.320]   of deals of varying L.
