[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.240]   While 10% is indeed high, it makes the math easier for the example,
[00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.840]   that is, the 3-year cost is $331 versus $300.
[00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.040]   In reality, I think 5-6% is more reasonable,
[00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:14.800]   though it's always easier to reduce something than increase it in a negotiation.
[00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.520]   Especially if your competition primes them by saying,
[00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.760]   "Those guys are in financial trouble, they need cash,
[00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.480]   so they're going to ask you for a multi-year prepaid deal."
[00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:23.520]   Mark my words.
