[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.960]   That is, that a 79% three-year rate is Ergo better than a one-year 90% renewal rate,
[00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.960]   arguing that while the buyer will get to recognize the deferred revenue over time that the cash has
[00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.960]   already been collected, and Ergo that the purchase price should be reduced by the cost of delivering
[00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:18.720]   that revenue, that is, COGS as per intern deferred revenue. Happily, the deferred revenue write-down
[00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.280]   approach seems to be in the midst of reevaluation.
