[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.240]   If the acquired company does a high percentage of multi-year prepaid deals and you write off its
[00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:08.400]   deferred revenue, it will certainly reduce its apparent growth rate and possibly cause it to
[00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.960]   shrink on a year-over-year basis. What was in the bag revenue for the acquired company gets
[00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.520]   vaporized for the acquirer. Or are other subsidiaries for a strategic acquirer?
[00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:22.160]   Known either as billings or calculated billings, I prefer the latter because it emphasizes that
[00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.560]   it's not a metric that most companies publish but one commonly derived by financial analysts,
[00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.360]   but one commonly derived by financial analysts.
