[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000]   We are testing the limits of my accounting knowledge here. But I suppose if deferred
[00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.440]   revenue is split into current and long-term, you might still be able to get a reasonable
[00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:12.000]   guesstimate for new ARR sales by calculating billings based only on current. But I'm not
[00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000]   sure that's true and worried that the constant flow from long-term to current deferred revenue
[00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.440]   will impede that analysis.
