[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800]   A purest SaaS company, and they do exist, would actually see two problems.
[00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.040]   First, potential year-over-year shrinkage due to the write-down discussed in footnote.
[00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:13.120]   Second, they'd face a dilemma in choosing between the risk associated with immediately
[00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:17.440]   transitioning the acquired company's business to annual only and the potential pollution
[00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:20.680]   of its otherwise pristine deferred revenue if they don't.
[00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.800]   Minute 1028 of the same video referenced in the prior link.
