[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.880]   This is an audio version of a Dave Kellogg post from May 3rd, 2019, titled "My Final
[00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:12.440]   Verdict on Multi-Year, Prepaid Deals," revised May 4th, 2019, 10,041 AM.
[00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:16.720]   After years of experience with and thinking about multi-year, prepaid SaaS deals, my mental
[00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:18.800]   jury is back in the box and the verdict is in.
[00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:22.520]   If you're a startup that is within my assumptions set below, don't do them.
[00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:26.720]   Before jumping in, let me first define precisely what I mean by multi-year, prepaid deals,
[00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:30.640]   and second, detail the assumptions behind my logic in response to some Twitter conversations
[00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:32.780]   I've had this morning about this post.
[00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:35.280]   What do I mean by multi-year, prepaid deals?
[00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.520]   While there are many forms of multi-year, prepaid deals, when I use the term, I am thinking
[00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:42.860]   primarily of a three-year agreement that is fully prepaid.
[00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:48.060]   For example, if a customer's ARR cost is 100 units for a one-year deal, you might approach
[00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:53.660]   them saying something akin to, "By default, our annual contracts have a 10% annual increase
[00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:54.960]   built in."
[00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:00.320]   If you sign and prepay a three-year agreement, that is, pay me 300 units within 60 days,
[00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:03.720]   then I will lock you in at the 100 units per year price.
[00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:07.460]   Some people didn't know these kinds of deals were possible, they are.
[00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:11.880]   In my experience, particularly for high-consideration purchases, where the customer has completed
[00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:16.000]   a thorough evaluation and is quite sure the system will work, a fairly high percentage
[00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.880]   of buyers will engage in this conversation.
