[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.480]   With such vast amounts of money in play, some say it's a growth-at-all-cost scheme,
[00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:08.720]   but others hold to the Rule of 40 which attempts to balance growth and profitability with a simple
[00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:13.120]   rule. Grow as fast as you want as long as your revenue growth rate plus your free cash flow
[00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:18.000]   margin, 40%. The Rule of 40 gets a lot of attention, but I think that companies are not
[00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.240]   asking the right question about it. The right question is not, "When should my growing startup
[00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.760]   be Rule of 40 compliant?"
