[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.480]   So, unless you're an absolutely amazing company like Elastic, which had a Rule of 40 score
[00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:09.240]   of 87% at its IPO, you probably shouldn't be unrealistically planning to become Rule
[00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.320]   of 40 compliant, three years before your IPO.
[00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.400]   If you do, especially if you're well-funded and don't need additional expense constraints,
[00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.000]   you might well compromise growth with a premature focus on the Rule of 40, which could shoot
[00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.400]   off your corporate foot in terms of your eventual valuation.
[00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.040]   If "When should we be Rule of 40 compliant?" is the wrong question then, "When should
[00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.400]   Should we be rule of 40 compliant is the wrong question.
