[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.320]   What should my company's rule of 40 glide slope be? That is, over the next several years,
[00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:08.240]   what is your eventual rule of 40 score target and how do you want to evolve to it?
[00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:12.240]   The big advantage of this question is that the answer isn't a year, and it doesn't assume rule
[00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:17.120]   of 40 compliance. But it does get you to start thinking about and tracking your rule of 40 score.
[00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.800]   I built a little model to help do some what-if analysis around this question.
[00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:22.000]   You can download it here.
