[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.640]   In our example, we've got a 5-year-old, $30 million ARR SaaS company planning the
[00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:10.560]   next 5 years of its evolution, hopefully with an IPO in year 8 or 9. The driver sells orange
[00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:14.320]   to find how fast you want to grow and what you want your rule of 40 glide slope to be.
[00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:18.720]   Everything else is calculated. At the bottom, we have an overall efficiency analysis,
[00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.720]   in each year how much more we're spending than the previous year, how much more revenue do we
[00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:26.560]   expect to get, and what's the ratio between the two, that is, which works like kind of an
[00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:31.360]   an incremental revenue, CAC, as we improve the role of 40 Glideslope to be.
