[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.200]   In the above CFO nightmare scenario, we hold expenses constant with the original plan and
[00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.600]   come in considerably lighter on revenue. The drives us miles off our desired rule
[00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:15.440]   of 40 glide slope, see red cells. We end up needing to fund $40-24 million more in operating
[00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:21.200]   losses than the original plan, all to generate a company that's $30.5 million smaller in revenue
[00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:26.480]   and generating much larger losses. It's no wonder why CFOs worry about this. They should.
[00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.800]   What would the CFO really like? A Rule of 40 Driven Autopilot.
