[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000]   In this post, we've talked about the rule of 40 and why startups should think about it as a glide slope rather than a short or mid-term destination.
[00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.000]   We've provided you with a downloadable model where you can play with your rule of 40 glide slope,
[00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.000]   and we've shown why CFOs will inherently be drawn to the rule of 40 as a long-term planning constraint,
[00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000]   because in many ways, it will help your company act like a self-riding ship.
[00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.000]   As in many ways, it will help your company act.
[00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:30.000]   Notes the 75th percentile spends $1.92, and 25% spend more than not, per key banks.
