[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.080]   I'm trying to find data, a good data set, of Rule of 40 scores at IPO time but thus
[00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:08.560]   far haven't found one. Anecdotally, I can say that lots of successful high-growth SaaS
[00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:13.600]   IPOs - for example, MongoDB, AnaPlan, and Blackline - were not Rule of 40 compliant
[00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:18.440]   at IPO time, nor were they well after, for example, as of October 2018 per JMP's quarterly
[00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:22.400]   software review. It seems that if growth is sufficiently there, that the profitability
[00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.660]   constraint can be somewhat deferred in the mind of the market.
