[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.120]   In a small startup, the CEO fills this gap. That's fine. The CEO should be the chief
[00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:09.760]   storyteller when the company is young and the product line is simple. But as the company grows,
[00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:14.960]   scales, and adds products, the CEO can no longer own this story in any operational sense. It
[00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.760]   becomes nobody's job, which means it either doesn't get done or gets done by someone pinch-hitting in
[00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:25.680]   the role. For example, the VP of brand doing their best, one of the product marketing VP's moonlighting.
