[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800]   the standard sales deck and demo. Someone has to own the pitch that walks a prospect through the
[00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.280]   whole portfolio story. If three product teams each own a piece of it, you don't have a deck,
[00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:14.160]   you have a Franken deck. Owning the sales deck is obvious. What's less obvious is that product line
[00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.080]   marketing should also own the standard demo, because the demo is just the same story told
[00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:22.320]   with a product as the visual instead of slides. If the deck and the demo tell different stories,
[00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:26.080]   you have a problem. They should be the same narrative expressed in two different stories,
[00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:30.320]   you have a problem, they should be the same narrative, expressed in two different media.
