[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.320]   Social media Maintaining a consistent social presence
[00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:08.760]   is too important to leave to chance, and too expensive to duplicate across product teams.
[00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:12.980]   Individual PMMs can and should contribute to social conversations in their area, but
[00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:16.940]   owning and maintaining the social presence needs to be someone's actual job.
[00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:20.980]   Centralizing it in product line marketing delivers both economies of scale and consistency
[00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:22.180]   of message.
[00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:26.340]   The alternative - having each product team manage their own presence, or delegating it
[00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:31.460]   to a PR/COMS person whose instincts are corporate rather than product - produces the kind of
[00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:31.900]   "F"
