[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920]   What's new is that the org structures that made product line marketing unnecessary.
[00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:09.040]   Single product companies, integrated marketing teams, CMOs who owned both message and demand,
[00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:13.520]   are now widely being replaced by decomposed structures. More companies are going multi-product
[00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:18.960]   faster. More are moving product marketing into the product org. And as they do, the gap grows.
[00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:23.440]   The solution isn't to reverse the decomposition. Putting product marketing back under marketing
[00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:27.760]   doesn't necessarily produce better product marketing. The decomposition, in many cases,
[00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:28.800]   is the right call.
