[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.360]   First, let's look at the COSC rule of 40 regression. Recall that R-squared is a statistical
[00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.000]   measure that explains the dependence of the dependent variable, in this case, ev_multiple,
[00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.480]   on the independent variable, rule of 40_score. Here you can see that about 58% of the variation
[00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:20.480]   in enterprise value multiple is explained by rule of 40_score. You can intuit that by
[00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.600]   looking at the dots relative to the line. While there is clearly some linear correlation
[00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.760]   between the data, it's a long way from perfect, that is, lots of dots are pretty far from
[00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:29.280]   the line.
