[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.440]   Now, the fun part.
[00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:04.760]   Let's see the same regression against revenue growth alone.
[00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.920]   R-squared here is 51%.
[00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:12.180]   So the explanatory power of the Rule of 40 is only 7% higher than revenue growth alone.
[00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:16.040]   Probably still worth looking at, but it sure gets a lot of PR for explaining only an incremental
[00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:17.040]   7%.
[00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.640]   It could be worse, I suppose.
[00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.520]   Rule of 40 could have a lower R-squared than revenue growth alone.
[00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.720]   In fact, it did back in 2008 and in 2012.
