[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000]   In the vein, for some real fun, let's look at how this relationship has changed over time.
[00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.440]   The first thing you'll notice is that pre-2012 both last 12-month LTM revenue growth and the
[00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:14.080]   rule of 40 had far weaker explanatory power, I suspect because profitability played a more
[00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:19.440]   important role in the equation. In 2012, the explanatory power of both metrics doubled.
[00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:24.560]   In 2015 and 2018 the rule of 40 explained nearly 20% more than revenue growth alone.
[00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:29.680]   In 2017 and 2017, however, that's dropped to 7-8%.
