[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840]   I still think the Rule of 40 is a nice way to think about balancing growth versus profit
[00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:08.240]   and Rule of 40 compliant companies still command a disproportionate share of market value.
[00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:12.280]   But remember, its explanatory power has dropped in recent years and, if you're running an
[00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.800]   early or mid-stage startup, there is very little comparative data available on the Rule
[00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:19.440]   of 40 scores of today's giants when they were at early, or mid-stage scale.
[00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.160]   That's why I think early.
[00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:24.640]   And mid-stage startups need to think about the Rule of 40 in terms of glide slope planning.
