[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.240]   If calculated using subscription revenue growth, it's 137% plus 26% en11%, even more amazing.
[00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:12.720]   One thing I don't like about the fluidity of Rule of 40 calculations, as you can see here,
[00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.680]   is that depending on what might seem small nuances in calculations,
[00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:21.600]   you can produce a very broad range of scores. Here, from 55% to 137%.
