[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.760]   To me, this means ending day one with a strong valuation, the degree to which that is up
[00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:08.680]   or down from the opening price is really about how the bankers price the offer.
[00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:12.520]   I am not a financial analyst and do not make buy or sell recommendations.
[00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:14.040]   See my disclaimers here.
[00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.800]   In fact, it's actually a double bar.
[00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:19.120]   First, you need to have been successful enough to go public, and second, you need to clear
[00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.680]   the rule of 40.
[00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:24.280]   Despite a minority of public companies actually clearing this bar, financial analysts are
[00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:28.080]   quick to point out the minority who do command a disproportionate share of market cap.
