[00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:04.960]   successful enough to go public, and second, you need to clear the Rule of 40. Despite a minority
[00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:08.800]   of public companies actually clearing this bar, financial analysts are quick to point out the
[00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:13.520]   minority who do command a disproportionate share of market cap. And via the resultant R-squared
[00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:19.920]   score, to what extent does the Rule of 40 score explain or drive the EV/R multiple? If R-squared
[00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:24.720]   were 1.E, all the dots would fall on the least-squares fit line. Which continues with further
[00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:29.920]   analysis, breaking the Rule of 40 into four zones. This audio version was created by Grant Duncan and
[00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:32.960]   AI with permission from Dave.
