[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.040]   After the SaaS acre of early 2016, investors generally backed off a growth-at-all-cost
[00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.280]   mindset and started to value SaaS companies using an appropriate balance of growth and
[00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:14.840]   profitability. The question then became, what's appropriate? The answer was, the rule of 40.
[00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:19.360]   What's the rule of 40? Growth-repressed profit should be greater than or equal to 40%.
