[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.880]   As a quick demonstration of the exception to every rule principle, Tintry recently went public
[00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:11.520]   off 45% growth with 81% operating margins, reflecting a rule of 40 score of 36%, and a
[00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:15.760]   placement that would be off the chart in the underneath sense even if corrected for non-cash
[00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:20.640]   expenses. For those interested in company valuations, the more interesting chart is this one.
